[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Configured execution and startup contracts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONFIGURED-EXECUTION-GRID-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve authored times and advance fixed grids
STATEMENT: >>>
Fixed dyadic runs shall publish every requested endpoint exactly once through
the stop time within their authored step budget. Explicit accepted grids shall
retain distinct representable penultimate times even inside endpoint roundoff.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: fixed_dyadic_grid_advances_without_drift_or_missing_endpoints,
64Proptest cases seed2026111923; explicit_grid_retains_a_distinct_penultimate_time_within_stop_roundoff.
Uses an analytic6V resistive circuit through the actual LU provider.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONFIGURED-EXECUTION-STARTUP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve behavioral startup dependencies and account for work
STATEMENT: >>>
Admitted grounded memoryless behavioral chains shall seed dependencies before
dependent domain-sensitive expressions, preserving differential controls and
output polarity. Reported linear solves shall include actual seed-provider work.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: chained_behavioral_startup_obeys_polarity_domains_and_counts_seed_work
uses a reversed-declaration two-stage log chain, three common-mode translations,
both grounded output orientations and independently counted LU calls. No fixed
Newton iteration count or unrestricted behavioral profile is required.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONFIGURED-EXECUTION-RESTART-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Restore trapezoidal integration after startup
STATEMENT: >>>
A nonlinear trapezoidal run without source corners shall use backward Euler
at startup and trapezoidal endpoint balance on subsequent accepted intervals.
The restart report shall identify only intervals actually restarted.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: nonlinear_trapezoidal_startup_restarts_once_then_obeys_endpoint_balance
independently checks resistor/Shockley/constant-capacitance current balance
in amperes within1e-10A. This is a bounded scalar circuit, not all model families.
<<<
